    <decisions>
        <name>Should_Notify</name>
        <label>Should Notify?</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>242</locationY>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>No - stay silent</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Qualifies</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>formQualifies</leftValueReference>
                <operator>EqualTo</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <booleanValue>true</booleanValue>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_Template</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Qualifies</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Sends the single "your commitment is now fully paid" message when an installment plan is completed. Fires at the OPPORTUNITY level, once, when the remaining balance transitions to zero.

Why here and not on the Payment: the completion message is an Opportunity-level event, not a payment-level one. Sending it per payment duplicated it whenever one save cleared several installments - a deposit batch of two produced two "fully paid" emails (verified in JCRC-Dev 2026-08-18). Firing on the parent makes duplicates structurally impossible rather than guarded against. The per-installment message stays on Payment_Notify_Donor_On_Paid, which now deliberately stays silent when a payment clears the balance.

Entry uses a filter FORMULA rather than field filters because Amount Outstanding is a formula field and formula fields do not work in record-triggered entry filters in this org (JSI-87 gotcha).

Runs on the ASYNCHRONOUS after-commit path for the same reason as the payment flow: a donor-email failure must never be able to roll back a payment save.

Stays silent when the gift is not Pledge / Major Gift / Grant, has only one payment, or has no primary contact. A missing email template is deliberately NOT swallowed - it fails visibly, because a silent not-found path previously hid a missing template for a full day.

JSI-125 / Jason Ott.

Change Log:
-----------
2026-08-18 - Jason Ott - Created (JSI-125 duplicate-notification fix).</description>
    <environments>Default</environments>
    <formulas>
        <name>formQualifies</name>
        <dataType>Boolean</dataType>
        <expression>AND(
  OR({!Get_RecordType.DeveloperName} = &quot;Pledge&quot;,
     {!Get_RecordType.DeveloperName} = &quot;Major_Gift&quot;,
     {!Get_RecordType.DeveloperName} = &quot;Grant&quot;),
  {!$Record.npe01__Number_of_Payments__c} &gt; 1,
  {!$Record.Payments_Made_Count__c} &gt; 0,
  NOT(ISBLANK({!$Record.npsp__Primary_Contact__c}))
)</expression>
    </formulas>
    <interviewLabel>Opportunity Notify Final Payment {!$Flow.CurrentDateTime}</interviewLabel>
    <label>Opportunity - Notify Final Payment</label>
    <processType>AutoLaunchedFlow</processType>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_RecordType</name>
        <label>Get Record Type</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>134</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Should_Notify</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>Id</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <elementReference>$Record.RecordTypeId</elementReference>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>RecordType</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <recordLookups>
        <name>Get_Template</name>
        <label>Get Email Template</label>
        <locationX>176</locationX>
        <locationY>350</locationY>
        <assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>false</assignNullValuesIfNoRecordsFound>
        <connector>
            <targetReference>Send_Final_Payment_Notification</targetReference>
        </connector>
        <filterLogic>and</filterLogic>
        <filters>
            <field>DeveloperName</field>
            <operator>EqualTo</operator>
            <value>
                <stringValue>Pmt_Email_Final_Payment</stringValue>
            </value>
        </filters>
        <getFirstRecordOnly>true</getFirstRecordOnly>
        <object>EmailTemplate</object>
        <storeOutputAutomatically>true</storeOutputAutomatically>
    </recordLookups>
    <start>
        <locationX>50</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>true</doesRequireRecordChangedToMeetCriteria>
        <filterFormula>AND(
  {!$Record.npe01__Amount_Outstanding__c} = 0,
  {!$Record.npe01__Payments_Made__c} &gt; 0
)</filterFormula>
        <object>Opportunity</object>
        <recordTriggerType>Update</recordTriggerType>
        <scheduledPaths>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Get_RecordType</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <pathType>AsyncAfterCommit</pathType>
        </scheduledPaths>
        <triggerType>RecordAfterSave</triggerType>
    </start>
    <status>Active</status>
</Flow>
